# tally 2.3.1 R4, Q1.5, P2 (L §8.2 `held:`: it prints once per row and keys read, the periods it was read for
# merged into maximal runs): rd[pl] and rd[de] are read for six days, a gap at 2026-01-08; each key's row is one
# line, two runs. Keys are never merged. Before: one line per day read, twelve lines.
=== heldruns.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-01-31

source s "s"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..

index wk = day 2026-01-05..2026-01-11
index regions = [pl, de]

input fee: money PLN
input d0: date
input dx: date
input rd[r in regions]: date reading

move pay[d in wk where d != dx and last(rd[pl], d) == d0 and last(rd[de], d) == d0]: transfers
  on d
  at d
  leg cash from konto to shop amount fee

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  fee = 10.00 PLN
  d0 = 2026-01-02
  dx = 2026-01-08
  rd[pl] = 2026-01-02 at 2026-01-01
  rd[de] = 2026-01-02 at 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "w"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-31)
=== expect
q: 40.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-01-05]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-01-06]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-01-07]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-01-09]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-01-10]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-01-11]
  held: rd[de] = 2026-01-02 (v), read for 2026-01-05 .. 2026-01-07, 2026-01-09 .. 2026-01-11
  held: rd[pl] = 2026-01-02 (v), read for 2026-01-05 .. 2026-01-07, 2026-01-09 .. 2026-01-11
  cut 2026-01-31
